-- examples/checks/agg-shrug-given-cut.rofl — agg_cell_shrug_given_cut: a
-- wall that falls after the rules reading shrug fired (check_opt budget
-- 2500; the join over what they read is what runs out). A walled
-- evaluation's rows are not final and its hole says so: it is cut short and
-- answers what it reached, the wall's own shrug among its rows. It was once
-- refused, `shrug is read of $adhoc, which a rule that reads shrug leaves
-- without an answer`, because the wall's row had arrived after a reader of
-- every shrug fired; the plain evaluator here, the aggregate one in
-- agg-shrug-given-cut-count.rofl.
-- expect-row: hole[$kernel]($adhoc,budget_exhausted)
-- expect-row: shrug[$kernel]($adhoc,budget,spent(steps,
-- expect-row: shrug[$kernel](in(sgx_b,sgx_k(0)),given,concluded)
sgx_n(0).
sgx_n(Y) :- sgx_n(X), X < 60, Y is X + 1.
unknown[sgx_b](sgx_k(X)) :- sgx_n(X).
sgx_any(T, R) :- shrug(T, R, _).
sgx_two(T, U) :- sgx_any(T, _), sgx_any(U, _).
